# core-vendor.manifest — provenance for files vendored from
# agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core. Machine-read by
# test_migration_0014 and test_migration_0015. Do NOT hand-edit: regenerate by
# re-vendoring.
#
# The vendored files are byte-identical to core and carry NO local header —
# a header would itself break the byte-identity it claimed to record.
#
# core_commit is a COMMIT, not a branch: a core checkout is a live
# workspace and may sit mid-change on a feature branch, and origin/main
# can advance BETWEEN two commands. Resolve it ONCE and vendor every file
# from that one revision — a per-file rev-parse is how the gate and the
# harness ended up from different commits on 2026-07-25.
#
# ONE commit covers EVERY file listed, and every file this repo vendors from
# core is listed. Consistency among the entries present is not sufficient: a
# manifest naming two of four files is internally consistent while recording
# nothing about the two it omits.
#
# Advancing core_commit therefore means RE-VERIFYING the files already listed
# at the new revision, not just appending the new ones. 750da2e -> 60cd83f was
# verified this way: core#42 touched neither gate file, so both sha256s below
# are unchanged and the single-commit claim stays true rather than becoming a
# convenient fiction about files nobody re-checked.
core_repo=agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core
core_commit=60cd83f8d236b4ef8646976f547e17edafb53eeb
file=bin/openspec-change-gate.sh sha256=11056079fc6b3aca67d2e28603a8a21b7cb6ae353a63a569833ca34798133208
file=tools/change-gate-conformance.sh sha256=b3c2f6b284c5f8423ce583005358403734c9d133a92985671914ff17cdb4eae7
file=bin/reviewer-cli.sh sha256=32718bb98dbb343946f13747cdb208c6bd112beeeeb84b01e0677af5354b7ec6
file=tools/reviewer-cli-conformance.sh sha256=4e45150a2cc2c12c5d0a08e099e4a399858bf99ee5f4bf1434d62ca9279f6656
